  statement "Under the qualified implementation and exact execution binding, the analytic consequence together with the three acquired output predicates implies the requested selected-model runtime result.\nOriginal ground status: Assumed.\nEngineering scope: {\"system_boundary\":\"The stipulated three-node model and one reusable finite_bayes_diagnosis/1 operation under the operator-authorised native binding.\",\"configuration\":\"PS-DIAG/1 uses Fault->Alarm and Fault->HeartbeatLost with binary state order [0,1] and healthy-before-faulty parent columns. Parameters are p_fault=0.02, p_alarm_given_fault=0.95, p_alarm_given_healthy=0.05, p_loss_given_fault=0.8 and p_loss_given_healthy=0.1. The prepared image is sha256:5d317440653dd5a188223baff22644397cc2a1bd071183a12e9c4cb2f3688f7f with pgmpy 1.1.2.\",\"operating_conditions\":\"This adverse selected run uses Alarm=true and HeartbeatLost=false with the unchanged CPDs, exact finite inference and no data fitting or sampling. The original positive input remains separately retained; its accepted review scopes are not imported here.\",\"units\":\"All masses and posterior probabilities have unit 1. Completion predicates are boolean and ages are seconds.\",\"time_horizon\":\"This immutable controlled-model investigation accepts executions and actual assessments at maximum age 86400 seconds while preserving their original clocks.\",\"consequences\":\"Acceptance establishes only the requested controlled-model computation. Incorrect acceptance would misstate the conditional probability or whether the prescribed library calculation was performed.\"}"
  environment engarg_case
}

